         <notewidget width="723" x="10" noteType="0" y="150" usesdiagramusefillcolor="1" usesdiagramfillcolor="1" isinstance="0" fillcolor="none" height="284" linecolor="none" xmi.id="iM3PIGx0UNoA" usefillcolor="1" linewidth="none" font="Sans Serif,10,-1,5,50,0,0,0,0,0" text="Data structures of the CYBOI interpreter:&#xa;&#xa;part:&#xa;It contains a model which may be primitive data (like a number) or compound data (child parts).&#xa;The part keeps properties (meta information) about the model it points to.&#xa;Properties are always a (compound) part that contains other (property) parts.&#xa;Further, it keeps the type of the model and a unique name for it.&#xa;&#xa;item:&#xa;It ist just a pointer to data (an array) combined with the size (memory) and count (number of elements).&#xa;&#xa;array:&#xa;An allocated area in memory that contains values which may be accessed via indices.&#xa;&#xa;value:&#xa;Some primitive like an integer number, a double number, a void* pointer etc.&#xa;"/>
